{
    "word": "shadoof",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "19f79347-efd9-3cde-bd08-3a7de421efdc",
                "word": "shadoof",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4f1d9998-bbdc-4e2b-ae0e-852a261cf497",
                        "entry_id": "19f79347-efd9-3cde-bd08-3a7de421efdc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "shadoofs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "123ba2b9-b5c6-3ae1-b976-1113f1f8b43e",
                        "entry_id": "19f79347-efd9-3cde-bd08-3a7de421efdc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An ancient device used to gather water, consisting of a pivoted stick with a bucket on the end of it."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "de6eba3d-feb5-41dd-b14d-cfbac450d010",
                                "sense_id": "123ba2b9-b5c6-3ae1-b976-1113f1f8b43e",
                                "text": "The shadoof can be traced back 5,400 years, or to about 3500 B. C., and the indications are that it was considered an ancient device even at that remote time. It is much like the old-fashioned well sweep, consisting of a pivoted pole, supported on two uprights, at one end of which is suspended a rope or pole with a bucket at the lower end."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ab161e20-1d39-441e-b9b7-b723ad637009",
                        "source_entry_id": "19f79347-efd9-3cde-bd08-3a7de421efdc",
                        "source_sense_id": "123ba2b9-b5c6-3ae1-b976-1113f1f8b43e",
                        "source_sense_description": "device used to gather water",
                        "target_lang_word": "chadouf",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chadouf",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c52c4b5c-0a89-3d84-82f1-0a09e3a853ae",
                                        "entry_id": "663d2e0a-5172-3fee-b11f-90011940b1ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Appareil utilisé pour puiser l’eau au moyen d’un balancier ou bascule que l’on fait pivoter pour verser l’eau à proximité."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "280e2137-fa6b-485b-a33b-eb84a2b6cb8f",
                                                "sense_id": "c52c4b5c-0a89-3d84-82f1-0a09e3a853ae",
                                                "text": "Certains utilisent une invention récente, le chadouf, qui permet d’amener l’eau en accrochant un récipient au bout d’une perche que l’on fait basculer sur un gros poteau vertical."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03605dad-ebbf-4c41-a7bc-b1175e47c352",
                                                "sense_id": "c52c4b5c-0a89-3d84-82f1-0a09e3a853ae",
                                                "text": "Cependant les hommes travaillent aux chadoufs afin de pouvoir arroser les cultures toujours altérées sous ce ciel ardent qui les brûle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e07acae0-f279-4520-8106-ebe70a1033de",
                                                "sense_id": "c52c4b5c-0a89-3d84-82f1-0a09e3a853ae",
                                                "text": "En Égypte, la puisette utilisée pour recueillir l'eau avec le chadouf est souvent un delou."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "975945a9-a15b-4482-9e13-964b404ed91c",
                                                "sense_id": "c52c4b5c-0a89-3d84-82f1-0a09e3a853ae",
                                                "text": "Dans l’angle supérieur gauche, un serviteur actionne le chadouf, système traditionnel égyptien pour puiser l’eau, car l’eau est un élément indispensable à la survie du mort."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "80129092-7f56-4a29-b5d9-c898f6f6770a",
